# Interface elements

New shared interface pieces go in `packages/ui` as custom elements. Do not add a React component, a utility-class stylesheet, or a separate package for one control.

Use the `af-` prefix and style the tag, not a class:

```html
<af-theme name="dark">
  <af-heading level="2">Title</af-heading>
  <af-panel>Content</af-panel>
</af-theme>
```

```css
af-panel {
  padding: var(--af-space-4);
  background: var(--af-color-panel);
}
```

Register elements from `defineAppElements()`. Keep state on attributes, properties, and events.

Do not add tabs, accordions, graphs, calendars, modals, menus, routing, or animation until a consuming application needs that element.
